  <section|Established (author side, conditional on the ledger's
  inputs)><label|established-author-side-conditional-on-the-ledgers-inputs>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>All eleven chapters audited in full; one substantive gap (F1)
    repaired with a detailed proof that follows <verbatim|YM.Work.C28>;
    notation repairs N1\UN3.

    <item>With F1, every hypothesis of the reconstruction propositions
    (<verbatim|input:word-boundary>, <verbatim|eq:word-motion-input> and the
    translation hypothesis) is discharged inside C04 from C04 outputs, apart
    from the incoming edges in ledger.md.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Still open><label|still-open>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>The incoming edges E1\UE5, C03-to-C04-reflection-J,
    C14-to-C04-calibrated-actions, C14-to-C04-null-equality,
    C03-to-C04-unique-heat and the new C03-C14-to-C04-involution-identity
    (findings F2). Their producers must acknowledge the exact statements.

    <item>O1 (Williams theorem number, for G03), O2 (dependency note for
    G06), O3 (UniqueHeat in the endpoint, for G01).

    <item>No Lean elaboration was possible here.

    <item>Material edits invalidate the earlier agent review fingerprints of
    complex-heat, reconstruction, boundary-detection and spectral-measure in
    <verbatim|reviews/draft-review.md>; they need renewed independent review.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|For the independent reviewer (<verbatim|results/C04/review/>)><label|for-the-independent-reviewer-resultsc04review>

  Review at the hashes above. Priorities: (1) the proof of
  <verbatim|cor:word-motion-inputs> against <verbatim|Lean/YM/Work/C28.lean>,
  including what <verbatim|Urs>, <verbatim|Descends.ties> and
  <verbatim|Descends.commutes> contain; (2) whether the involution-identity
  requirement F2 is real and correctly stated; (3) that N1\UN3 introduced no
  inconsistency elsewhere (grep for <verbatim|\\mathcal V>, <verbatim|T_E>,
  <verbatim|\\tau_a>). Unchanged chapters may reuse earlier review evidence
  only after checking that their hashes are unchanged.

  <section|For the next author><label|for-the-next-author>

  The C04 author scope is complete as far as this session can tell. If a
  review returns substantive changes, the fixes belong to a new C04 author
  claim.

